None: your ticket names no repos yet. Don't change any repo's main
checkout. If the work needs a repo, add it to the ticket
(`{{.CLI}} ticket set {{.Ticket.ID}} --repo <name>`, every repo it touches,
primary first), and slop-bot makes its worktree and tells you where.
{{end -}}

**Read each repo's own instruction files** (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`,
whichever it has) before working in its worktree. Your harness may load
only one of those names, or only the primary repo's.

- Reuse these worktrees for everything this ticket needs, including more
  than one PR: cut a new branch in the same worktree for each, named
  `slop-bot/t{{.Ticket.ID}}/<name>`. slop-bot deletes those branches with the
  worktrees once their work is pushed, and tells the user about any other.
- Don't create worktrees elsewhere. slop-bot cleans these up when the ticket
  ends, and keeps any with uncommitted or unpushed work.

